From: wu <wuc8974@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 20:29:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] feat(pqc-m2): device-identity public API speaks
 ML-DSA-65 only
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PQC migration (whitepaper section 2.1): Ed25519 device identity is removed
from the runtime path. The public API in src/infra/device-identity.ts now
generates, stores, signs, and verifies ML-DSA-65 (FIPS 204) identities
exclusively; the legacy Ed25519 KAT is skipped with a whitepaper pointer.

- device-identity.ts: signDevicePayload / verifyDeviceSignature /
  publicKeyRawBase64UrlFromPem / deriveDeviceIdFromPublicKey /
  normalizeDevicePublicKeyBase64Url now operate on the MLDSA65-{PUBLIC,
  SECRET}-KEY prefixed base64url wire format produced by
  src/infra/mldsa65-key-storage.ts (M1).
- device-identity-store.ts: generateStoredDeviceIdentity generates an
  ML-DSA-65 keypair, keyPairMatches round-trips through sign/verify, and
  salvageStoredIdentityRow only accepts the new wire format (legacy Ed25519
  PEM rows fall through to the doctor-repair path that drops the bad row
  and writes a fresh ML-DSA-65 identity).
- device-identity.test.ts: existing Ed25519 KAT converted to it.skip with a
  whitepaper 2.1 reference; new ML-DSA-65 invariants cover prefix shape,
  public/raw round-trip, Ed25519-shaped bogus signature rejection, and
  signature length (3309 bytes).
- device-identity-store.test.ts: 9 invariants covering keypair shape,
  validate, repair of legacy Ed25519 rows, conflict preservation, and
  read-only missing-database path.

9/9 store + 17/17 public + 4 Ed25519-legacy skip = 26 invariants green
(M1 KAT remains 17/17 green).

